            <ArticleTitle>Behavioral model for diffuse noxious inhibitory controls (DNIC): potentiation by 5-hydroxytryptophan.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>461-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The effects of the serotonin precursor 5-HTP, were determined in a behavioral DNIC paradigm (increase in vocalization threshold after intraperitoneal injection of the algogenic agent, phenylbenzoquinone). This counter-irritation phenomenon was strongly potentiated by 5-HTP, such potentiation being blocked by the 5-HT receptor blocker, cinanserin. These results are in keeping with those of our recent single unit work in dorsal horn convergent neurons.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
